      "text": "Matisia cordata, known as the South American sapote or chupa-chupa, is a large, semi-deciduous fruit tree reaching heights of up to 45 meters. It is native to the Amazon rainforest vegetation in Bolivia, Brazil, Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru."
